3.6 Females of Reproductive Age (15 - 49 years)
Females aged 15 - 49 form a special group of the population due to their role in reproduction.
Nearly half of the female population (47.3 percent) in Tanzania is in the Reproductive Age
(15 - 49 years). For Tanzania Mainland, 47.2 percent of women were in reproductive ages
and the corresponding figure for Tanzania Zanzibar was 50.4 percent. Dar es Salam Region
had the highest proportion of women of childbearing age (60.9 percent), followed by Mjini
Magharibi Region (54.0 percent) and Kusini Unguja Region (52.3 percent). Regions with
lowest proportion of women of reproductive age were Simiyu and Singida with 41.0 and
41.5 percent respectively (Map 3.4).
