3.7.1 Population Living in Urban Areas
The proportion of the population living in urban areas increased by five percent during the
intercensal period. Figure 3.20 reveals that, population living in urban areas has increased
significantly from 23.1 percent in 2002 to 34.9 percent in 2022 for the United Republic of
Tanzania. A similar pattern is portrayed in Tanzania Mainland and Tanzania Zanzibar.
